/-!
# Literal native rows in the marked point-core intersection

These twenty-six subgroups use the original max2 `kernelProduct` words.
Indices 0--15 are the saved eight configurations, in the retained diagnostic's
order; indices 16--25 are its sixteen configurations. In particular index 5
is the line candidate and index 14 is the previously certified non-line eight.
The definitions are independent of whole-normalizer placement and of the
still separate proof that the list exhausts all eligible marked subgroups.

The literal marked points are the original central involution `t` and
`sourceP`; no additional marking assumption is built into the definitions.
Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Corollary 1.2.2(a), Section 2.1, pp.488--489,
and the native max2/max4 words in the imported ATLAS source directories.
-/

public noncomputable section
open Subgroup Theory.GroupTheory
namespace Janko4.LocalStructure.PureFirstNormalizers.AllRowTwo.FiniteConfigurations
open OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData
open LowerBound
open CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter1.Terminal.LinearFourActions.JankoFourStabilizer.Max1Placement.SylowCover.MatrixNormalizerBounds.Max4EightCentralizer

/-- The actual first marked point used by `MarkedIntersection`. -/
@[expose] def markedT : Model := t

/-- The actual second marked point, the native kernel word with mask 6607. -/
@[expose] def markedP : Model := sourceP

/-- The literal native word attached to a thirteen-bit kernel mask. -/
@[expose] def nativeWord (m : Fin 8192) : Model := kernelProduct m

/-- Complete literal mask sets, retaining the saved order of the configurations. -/
@[expose] def rowMasks : Fin 26 → Finset (Fin 8192) := ![
  {0,1,1578,1579,6606,6607,8164,8165},
  {0,1,2390,2391,4248,4249,6606,6607},
